IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc6-builders`

-- ccc6-bestiality.l4 -- s 160, Bestiality: the offences, the defence of public good, the court's orders, the breach of an order, and the definition of bestiality.
-- Where a limb says "or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction" and states no penalty, the punishment function takes the penalty of s 787(1) as an input (another part).

§ `s 160 Bestiality`

-- src:3129 | Definition of bestiality
-- src:3130 | (7) In this section, bestiality means any contact, for a sexual purpose, with an animal.
@ref Criminal Code s 160(7) (src:3129-3130)
GIVEN `there was contact with an animal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contact was for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(7) bestiality` MEANS
    IF `there was contact with an animal` AND `the contact was for a sexual purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "bestiality means any contact, for a sexual purpose, with an animal"

-- src:3101 | Bestiality
-- src:3102 | 160 (1) Every person who commits bestiality is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 160(1) (src:3101-3102)
GIVEN `there was contact with an animal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contact was for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(1) the conduct is the offence of bestiality` MEANS
    IF `s 160(7) bestiality` `there was contact with an animal` `the contact was for a sexual purpose` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who commits bestiality is guilty of an indictable offence"

@ref Criminal Code s 160(1) (src:3102)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 160(1) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 160(1) (src:3102)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 160(1) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 160(1) (src:3101-3102)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 160(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:3103 | Compelling the commission of bestiality
-- src:3104 | (2) Every person who compels another to commit bestiality is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 160(2) (src:3103-3104)
GIVEN `the person compelled another person to commit an act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 160(7) bestiality` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(2) the conduct is the offence of compelling the commission of bestiality` MEANS
    IF `the person compelled another person to commit an act` AND `s 160(7) bestiality` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who compels another to commit bestiality is guilty of an indictable offence"

@ref Criminal Code s 160(2) (src:3104)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 160(2) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 160(2) (src:3104)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 160(2) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 160(2) (src:3103-3104)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 160(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

DECLARE `s 160(3) what the person did` IS ONE OF
    `s 160(3) committed bestiality in the presence of a person under the age of 16 years`
    `s 160(3) incited a person under the age of 16 years to commit bestiality`
    `s 160(3) neither`

-- src:3105 | Bestiality in presence of or by child
-- src:3106 | (3) Despite subsection (1), every person who commits bestiality in the presence of a person under the age of 16 years, or who incites a person under the age of 16 years to commit bestiality,
-- src:3107 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of one year; or
-- src:3108 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of six months.
@ref Criminal Code s 160(3) (src:3105-3108)
GIVEN `what the person did` IS A `s 160(3) what the person did`
      `the age in years of the person in whose presence the act was done, or who was incited` IS A NUMBER
      `s 160(7) bestiality` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(3) the conduct is the offence of bestiality in the presence of, or by inciting, a person under 16` MEANS
    IF    NOT (`what the person did` EQUALS `s 160(3) neither`)
      AND `the age in years of the person in whose presence the act was done, or who was incited` LESS THAN 16
      AND `s 160(7) bestiality` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every person who commits bestiality in the presence of a person under the age of 16 years, or who incites a person under the age of 16 years to commit bestiality"

@ref Criminal Code s 160(3)(a) (src:3107)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 160(3)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 160(3)(b) (src:3108)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 160(3)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`, `imprisonment for a term of` `six months`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 160(3) (src:3105-3108)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 160(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

DECLARE `s 160(3.1) what the person did with the visual representation` IS ONE OF
    `s 160(3.1) publishes`
    `s 160(3.1) distributes`
    `s 160(3.1) transmits`
    `s 160(3.1) sells`
    `s 160(3.1) makes available`
    `s 160(3.1) advertises`
    `s 160(3.1) none of those`

-- src:3109 | Representation of bestiality
-- src:3110 | (3.1) Every person commits an offence who knowingly publishes, distributes, transmits, sells, makes available or advertises any visual representation that is or is likely to be mistaken for a photographic, film, video or other visual recording of a person committing bestiality.
@ref Criminal Code s 160(3.1) (src:3109-3110)
GIVEN `the person acted knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the person did` IS A `s 160(3.1) what the person did with the visual representation`
      `it is a visual representation that is or is likely to be mistaken for a photographic, film, video or other visual recording of a person committing bestiality` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(3.1) the conduct is the offence of publishing or distributing a representation of bestiality` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted knowingly`
      AND NOT (`what the person did` EQUALS `s 160(3.1) none of those`)
      AND `it is a visual representation that is or is likely to be mistaken for a photographic, film, video or other visual recording of a person committing bestiality`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person commits an offence who knowingly publishes, distributes, transmits, sells, makes available or advertises any visual representation that is or is likely to be mistaken for a photographic, film, video or other visual recording of a person committing bestiality"

-- (3.2) "No person shall be convicted of an offence under subsection (3.1) if the conduct ... served the public good and did not extend beyond what served the public good."
-- src:3111 | Defence of public good
-- src:3112 | (3.2) No person shall be convicted of an offence under subsection (3.1) if the conduct that forms the subject-matter of the charge served the public good and did not extend beyond what served the public good.
@ref Criminal Code s 160(3.2) (src:3111-3112)
GIVEN `the conduct that forms the subject-matter of the charge served the public good` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct did not extend beyond what served the public good` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(3.2) section 160 gives a defence of public good against a charge under subsection (3.1)` MEANS
    IF `the conduct that forms the subject-matter of the charge served the public good` AND `the conduct did not extend beyond what served the public good`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be convicted of an offence under subsection (3.1) if the conduct that forms the subject-matter of the charge served the public good and did not extend beyond what served the public good"

DECLARE `s 160(3.3) the question` IS ONE OF
    `s 160(3.3) whether the conduct served the public good`
    `s 160(3.3) whether there is evidence that the conduct alleged went beyond what served the public good`
    `s 160(3.3) whether the conduct did or did not extend beyond what served the public good`
    `s 160(3.3) another question`

-- src:3113 | Question of law and fact, motives
-- src:3114 | (3.3) For the purposes of subsection (3.2),
-- src:3115 | (a) it is a question of law whether the conduct served the public good and whether there is evidence that the conduct alleged went beyond what served the public good, but it is a question of fact whether the conduct did or did not extend beyond what served the public good; and
-- src:3116 | (b) the motives of the accused are irrelevant.
@ref Criminal Code s 160(3.3) (src:3113-3116)
GIVEN question IS A `s 160(3.3) the question`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(3.3)(a) the question is a question of law` MEANS
    CONSIDER question
    WHEN `s 160(3.3) whether the conduct served the public good` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 160(3.3) whether there is evidence that the conduct alleged went beyond what served the public good` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 160(3.3) whether the conduct did or did not extend beyond what served the public good` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but it is a question of fact whether the conduct did or did not extend beyond what served the public good"
    WHEN `s 160(3.3) another question` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of subsection (3.2), (a) it is a question of law whether the conduct served the public good and whether there is evidence"

@ref Criminal Code s 160(3.3)(b) (src:3116)
GIVEN `the matter is the motives of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(3.3)(b) the motives of the accused are relevant` MEANS
    IF `the matter is the motives of the accused`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the motives of the accused are irrelevant"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (b) says nothing of any matter but the accused's motives

-- src:3117 | Punishment — representation of bestiality
-- src:3118 | (3.4) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (3.1)
-- src:3119 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:3120 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 160(3.4) (src:3117-3120)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 160(3.4)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 160(3.4)(b) (src:3120)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 160(3.4)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 160(3.4) (src:3117-3120)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 160(3.4) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (4) The court "may, in addition to any other sentence that it may impose under any of subsections (1) to (3) and (3.4)": a power of the court. Its gates are limits in its own wording: a case outside them is NOTHING.
DECLARE `s 160(4)(a) what the order prohibits` IS ONE OF
    `s 160(4)(a) owning an animal`
    `s 160(4)(a) having the custody or control of an animal`
    `s 160(4)(a) residing in the same premises as an animal`
    `s 160(4)(a) something else`

-- src:3121 | Order of prohibition or restitution
-- src:3122 | (4) The court may, in addition to any other sentence that it may impose under any of subsections (1) to (3) and (3.4),
-- src:3123 | (a) make an order prohibiting the accused from owning, having the custody or control of or residing in the same premises as an animal during any period that the court considers appropriate but, in the case of a second or subsequent offence, for a minimum of five years; and
-- src:3124 | (b) on application of the Attorney General or on its own motion, order that the accused pay to a person or an organization that has taken care of an animal as a result of the commission of the offence the reasonable costs that the person or organization incurred in respect of the animal, if the costs are readily ascertainable.
@ref Criminal Code s 160(4) (src:3121-3124)
GIVEN `the accused is sentenced under subsection (1), (2), (3) or (3.4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the order prohibits` IS A `s 160(4)(a) what the order prohibits`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(4)(a) the court may make an order prohibiting the accused` MEANS
    IF    `the accused is sentenced under subsection (1), (2), (3) or (3.4)`
      AND NOT (`what the order prohibits` EQUALS `s 160(4)(a) something else`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in addition to any other sentence that it may impose under any of subsections (1) to (3) and (3.4), (a) make an order prohibiting the accused from owning, having the custody or control of or residing in the same premises as an animal"

-- "during any period that the court considers appropriate but, in the case of a second or subsequent offence, for a minimum of five years": a minimum of five years for a second or subsequent offence; none is stated otherwise.
@ref Criminal Code s 160(4)(a) (src:3123)
GIVEN `the offence is a second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Length of time`)
`s 160(4)(a) the shortest period of the order` MEANS
    IF `the offence is a second or subsequent offence`
    THEN JUST `five years`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no minimum period is stated for a first offence ("during any period that the court considers appropriate")

@ref Criminal Code s 160(4)(b) (src:3124)
-- LIMB BY LIMB (sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F9): the application / own-motion limb is a gate of the upon kind, so a failed application / own-motion limb answers as the guide does (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05): JUST FALSE, listed in the fork register with the other reading (NOTHING). The other limbs are if-gates or scope limits and answer NOTHING (11-12 limit (1); ruling (c) of 2026-11-05).
GIVEN `the accused is sentenced under subsection (1), (2), (3) or (3.4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General applied, or the court acts on its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person or an organization has taken care of an animal as a result of the commission of the offence and incurred reasonable costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs are readily ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(4)(b) the court may order the accused to pay the reasonable costs of the animal's care` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Attorney General applied, or the court acts on its own motion`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of the Attorney General or on its own motion"
        IF    `the accused is sentenced under subsection (1), (2), (3) or (3.4)`
          AND `a person or an organization has taken care of an animal as a result of the commission of the offence and incurred reasonable costs`
          AND `the costs are readily ascertainable`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on application of the Attorney General or on its own motion, order that the accused pay to a person or an organization that has taken care of an animal as a result of the commission of the offence the reasonable costs that the person or organization incurred in respect of the animal, if the costs are readily ascertainable"

-- src:3125 | Breach of order
-- src:3126 | (5) Every person who contravenes an order made under paragraph (4)(a) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 160(5) (src:3125-3126)
GIVEN `the person contravened an order made under paragraph (4)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(5) the conduct is the offence of contravening an order made under paragraph (4)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the person contravened an order made under paragraph (4)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who contravenes an order made under paragraph (4)(a) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction"

@ref Criminal Code s 160(5) (src:3126)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 160(5) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 160(5) (src:3125-3126)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 160(5) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:3127 | Application
-- src:3128 | (6) Sections 740 to 741.2 apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to orders made under paragraph (4)(b).
@ref Criminal Code s 160(6) (src:3127-3128)
GIVEN `the order is made under paragraph (4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(6) sections 740 to 741.2 apply to the order` MEANS
    IF `the order is made under paragraph (4)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sections 740 to 741.2 apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to orders made under paragraph (4)(b)"
